/-!
# A perfect generator for `D_{QCoh,T}(𝒪_{Spec A})`

Let `A` be a commutative ring and let `T ⊆ Spec A` be a closed subset whose complement is
quasi-compact. The category `D_{QCoh,T}(𝒪_{Spec A})` of complexes with quasi-coherent cohomology
supported on `T` is weakly generated by a single perfect object, namely the sheafified Koszul
complex of a finite sequence `f₁, …, f_r ∈ A` cutting `T` out of `Spec A`.

The generator is `Stacks.Koszul.Truncation.koszulObject f`, and the three things asked of it are
each already available for it:

* it is perfect, by `Stacks.Koszul.Truncation.isPerfect_koszulObject`;
* its cohomology is quasi-coherent, because a perfect object of `D(𝒪_X)` has quasi-coherent
  cohomology (`Stacks.DerivedQCoh.AnyModel.isDQCoh_of_isPerfect`), and supported on `T`, because
  it restricts to zero on `D(f₁) ∪ … ∪ D(f_r) = Spec A ∖ T`
  (`Stacks.Koszul.OpenComplement.isZero_derivedRestrict_koszulObject`);
* it detects the zero object, by [Stacks, Tag 09IR] in the form
  `Stacks.Koszul.Truncation.isZero_of_forall_hom_koszulObject_eq_zero`.

The support hypothesis is what makes the detection unconditional. Tag 09IR detects the zero
object of `D_QCoh(𝒪_{Spec A})` from *two* hypotheses: orthogonality to the shifts of the Koszul
object, and vanishing of the restriction to `U = D(f₁) ∪ … ∪ D(f_r)`. For an object of
`D_{QCoh,T}(𝒪_{Spec A})` the second hypothesis is automatic, because `U` is exactly the complement
of the supporting set `T` and a complex supported on `T` restricts to zero there.

## Main results

* `Stacks.Rouquier.exists_openComplement_eq_compl` — a closed subset of `Spec A` with
  quasi-compact complement is the common zero locus of a finite sequence, in the
  `Stacks.Koszul.Truncation.openComplement` spelling of that complement.
* `Stacks.Rouquier.quasiCoherentSupported_koszulObject` — the Koszul object of a sequence cutting
  out `T` lies in `D_{QCoh,T}(𝒪_{Spec A})`.
* `Stacks.Rouquier.isZero_of_subsingleton_hom_koszulObject` — the detection statement: an object
  of `D_{QCoh,T}(𝒪_{Spec A})` orthogonal to every shift of the Koszul object is zero.
* `Stacks.Rouquier.exists_isPerfect_generator_supported_spec` — the three together: on `Spec A`
  there is a perfect object of `D_{QCoh,T}(𝒪_{Spec A})` which detects its zero object.
* `Stacks.Rouquier.exists_isPerfect_isWeakTriangulatedGenerator_supported_spec` — the same read as
  `CategoryTheory.ObjectProperty.IsWeakTriangulatedGenerator` of a singleton inside
  `D_{QCoh,T}(𝒪_{Spec A})`.

## Implementation notes

Tag 0A9A is the statement for a quasi-compact quasi-separated *scheme*; what is proved here is its
affine case, on `Spec A` literally.

The derived category is the locally small model of
`StacksFrontier/Homology/DerivedCategory/LocallySmall.lean`: no
`CategoryTheory.HasDerivedCategory` binder appears below, so instance search supplies the global
instances. The detection statement
`Stacks.Koszul.Truncation.isZero_of_forall_hom_koszulObject_eq_zero` passes through the affine
derived Spec–Γ equivalence of [Stacks, Tag 06Z0], which is available at this model, and weak
generation is read through right-orthogonality, which has content only in a model whose morphisms
lie in the universe indexing the direct sums of `𝒪_X`-modules.

`Stacks.Cohomology.PushforwardRestriction.CohomologySupportedOn` and
`Stacks.Duality.derivedSupported` are the same notion — vanishing of the stalks of the cohomology
sheaves off `T` — spelled with two different stalk functors; the two implications between them
are proved below.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0A9A](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0A9A)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 09IR](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/09IR)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 09IS](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/09IS)
* [Rouquier, Theorem 6.8, *Dimensions of triangulated categories*]
-/

-- This file uses the locally small derived-category models below, which are not
-- global instances (see `StacksFrontier.Homology.DerivedCategory.LocallySmall`):
-- `D(R)` for sheaves of modules on a small site.
-- `D(𝒪_X)` for a scheme.
attribute [local instance] SheafOfModules.hasDerivedCategory
attribute [local instance] AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.hasDerivedCategory

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits CategoryTheory.ObjectProperty
open TopologicalSpace
open Stacks.Cohomology.PushforwardRestriction
open Stacks.Cohomology.PerfectComplexes (IsPerfect)
open Stacks.Koszul.Truncation (koszulObject openComplement)

universe u

namespace Stacks.Rouquier

/-! ### The two spellings of cohomological support -/

section Bridge

variable {X : TopCat.{u}} (O : Sheaf (Opens.grothendieckTopology X) RingCat.{u}) (T : Set X)
  [HasDerivedCategory.{u} (SheafOfModules.{u} O)]

/-- The `Stacks.Cohomology.PushforwardRestriction.CohomologySupportedOn` spelling of support
implies the `Stacks.Duality.derivedSupported` one. Both say that the stalks of all the cohomology
sheaves vanish outside `T`. -/
theorem derivedSupported_of_cohomologySupportedOn
    (E : DerivedCategory (SheafOfModules.{u} O)) (hE : CohomologySupportedOn O T E) :
    Stacks.Duality.derivedSupported O T E :=
  fun n x hx => hE n x hx

/-- The `Stacks.Duality.derivedSupported` spelling of support implies the
`Stacks.Cohomology.PushforwardRestriction.CohomologySupportedOn` one, the converse of
`Stacks.Rouquier.derivedSupported_of_cohomologySupportedOn`. -/
theorem cohomologySupportedOn_of_derivedSupported
    (E : DerivedCategory (SheafOfModules.{u} O))
    (hE : Stacks.Duality.derivedSupported O T E) :
    CohomologySupportedOn O T E :=
  fun n x hx => hE n x hx

end Bridge

/-! ### Restricting a supported complex to an open away from its support -/

/-- **A complex supported on `T` restricts to zero on an open disjoint from `T`.** -/
theorem isZero_derivedRestrict_of_derivedSupported {X : Scheme.{u}} (T : Set X) (U : X.Opens)
    (hU : (U : Set X) ⊆ Tᶜ) (E : DerivedCategory X.Modules)
    (hE : Stacks.Duality.derivedSupported X.ringCatSheaf T E) :
    IsZero ((Stacks.Duality.OpenImmersion.derivedRestrict U.ι).obj E) := by
  have hL : PreservesFiniteLimits (Scheme.Modules.restrictFunctor U.ι) := inferInstance
  have hC : PreservesFiniteColimits (Scheme.Modules.restrictFunctor U.ι) := inferInstance
  have hpre := @Stacks.DerivedQCoh.cohomologySupportedOn_derivedRestriction _ X.ringCatSheaf U T
    (Scheme.Modules.restrictFunctor U.ι)
    (Stacks.Duality.OpenImmersion.jStar_eq_restrictFunctor X U).symm
    (Scheme.Modules.restrictFunctor_additive U.ι) hL hC _
    (cohomologySupportedOn_of_derivedSupported X.ringCatSheaf T E hE)
  exact Stacks.DerivedQCoh.isZero_of_cohomologySupportedOn_empty _ _
    fun i y _ => hpre i y fun h => hU y.2 h

/-! ### The supporting set of a closed subset with quasi-compact complement -/

/-- **A closed subset of `Spec A` with quasi-compact complement is cut out by a finite sequence**:
its complement is the `Stacks.Koszul.Truncation.openComplement` `D(f₁) ∪ … ∪ D(f_r)` of a finite
sequence. -/
theorem exists_openComplement_eq_compl {A : Type u} [CommRing A]
    (T : Set (Spec (CommRingCat.of A))) (hT : IsClosed T) (hTc : IsCompact Tᶜ) :
    ∃ (r : ℕ) (f : Fin r → A), (openComplement f : Set (Spec (CommRingCat.of A))) = Tᶜ := by
  obtain ⟨r, f, hrf⟩ := Stacks.DerivedQCoh.OpenLift.exists_unionOfBasicOpens_eq
    (A := CommRingCat.of A) ⟨Tᶜ, hT.isOpen_compl⟩ hTc
  refine ⟨r, f, ?_⟩
  have he : openComplement f = Koszul.DerivedSystem.unionOfBasicOpens (A := CommRingCat.of A) f :=
    iSup_congr fun i => AlgebraicGeometry.basicOpen_eq_of_affine (R := CommRingCat.of A) (f i)
  rw [he, hrf]
  rfl

/-! ### The Koszul object is a supported quasi-coherent complex -/

/-- **The Koszul object of `f₁, …, f_r` has quasi-coherent cohomology.** -/
theorem derivedQuasiCoherent_koszulObject {A : Type u} [CommRing A] {r : ℕ} (f : Fin r → A) :
    Stacks.Duality.derivedQuasiCoherent (Spec (CommRingCat.of A)) (koszulObject f) :=
  Stacks.DerivedQCoh.AnyModel.isDQCoh_of_isPerfect
    (AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.hasDerivedCategory (Spec (CommRingCat.of A))) _
    (Stacks.Koszul.Truncation.isPerfect_koszulObject f)

/-- **The Koszul object of `f₁, …, f_r` is supported on the complement of
`D(f₁) ∪ … ∪ D(f_r)`.** -/
theorem derivedSupported_koszulObject {A : Type u} [CommRing A] {r : ℕ} (f : Fin r → A)
    (T : Set (Spec (CommRingCat.of A)))
    (hfT : (openComplement f : Set (Spec (CommRingCat.of A))) = Tᶜ) :
    Stacks.Duality.derivedSupported (Spec (CommRingCat.of A)).ringCatSheaf T
      (koszulObject f) := by
  have := RingedSpace.restrictModules_additive.{u, u} (Spec (CommRingCat.of A)).toRingedSpace
    (openComplement (A := A) f)
  have := RingedSpace.restrictModules_preservesFiniteLimits.{u, u}
    (Spec (CommRingCat.of A)).toRingedSpace (openComplement (A := A) f)
  have := RingedSpace.restrictModules_preservesFiniteColimits.{u}
    (Spec (CommRingCat.of A)).toRingedSpace (openComplement (A := A) f)
  have hz := (Stacks.Koszul.OpenComplement.isZero_derivedRestrict_koszulObject f).of_iso
    ((Stacks.DerivedQCoh.AnyModel.derivedJStarIsoRestrictFunctor
      (Spec (CommRingCat.of A)) (openComplement (A := A) f)).app (koszulObject f))
  refine derivedSupported_of_cohomologySupportedOn _ _ _ ?_
  refine Stacks.DerivedQCoh.cohomologySupportedOn_mono _ ?_
    (Stacks.DerivedQCoh.cohomologySupportedOn_compl_of_isZero_restrict
      _ (openComplement (A := A) f) (koszulObject f) hz)
  intro y hy
  by_contra hyT
  exact hy (by rw [hfT]; exact hyT)

/-- **The Koszul object of a sequence cutting `T` out of `Spec A` lies in
`D_{QCoh,T}(𝒪_{Spec A})`.** -/
theorem quasiCoherentSupported_koszulObject {A : Type u} [CommRing A] {r : ℕ} (f : Fin r → A)
    (T : Set (Spec (CommRingCat.of A)))
    (hfT : (openComplement f : Set (Spec (CommRingCat.of A))) = Tᶜ) :
    Stacks.Duality.quasiCoherentSupported (Spec (CommRingCat.of A)) T (koszulObject f) :=
  ⟨derivedQuasiCoherent_koszulObject f, derivedSupported_koszulObject f T hfT⟩

/-! ### Detection of the zero object -/

/-- **The Koszul object detects the zero object of `D_{QCoh,T}(𝒪_{Spec A})`**: an object of
`D_{QCoh,T}(𝒪_{Spec A})` orthogonal to every shift of the Koszul object of a sequence cutting `T`
out of `Spec A` is zero. -/
theorem isZero_of_subsingleton_hom_koszulObject {A : Type u} [CommRing A] {r : ℕ} (f : Fin r → A)
    (T : Set (Spec (CommRingCat.of A)))
    (hfT : (openComplement f : Set (Spec (CommRingCat.of A))) = Tᶜ)
    (E : DerivedCategory (Spec (CommRingCat.of A)).Modules)
    (hE : Stacks.Duality.quasiCoherentSupported (Spec (CommRingCat.of A)) T E)
    (horth : ∀ n : ℤ, Subsingleton ((koszulObject f)⟦n⟧ ⟶ E)) :
    IsZero E := by
  refine Stacks.Koszul.Truncation.isZero_of_forall_hom_koszulObject_eq_zero f E hE.1 ?_
    fun n g => (horth n).allEq g 0
  exact isZero_derivedRestrict_of_derivedSupported T (openComplement (A := A) f) hfT.subset E hE.2

/-! ### The affine base case of [Stacks, Tag 0A9A] -/

/-- **The affine base case of [Stacks, Tag 0A9A].** Let `A` be a commutative ring and `T ⊆ Spec A`
a closed subset with quasi-compact complement. There is an object of `D(𝒪_{Spec A})` which lies in
`D_{QCoh,T}(𝒪_{Spec A})`, is perfect, and detects the zero object of `D_{QCoh,T}(𝒪_{Spec A})`: it
is the sheafified Koszul complex of a finite sequence cutting `T` out of `Spec A`. -/
theorem exists_isPerfect_generator_supported_spec {A : Type u} [CommRing A]
    (T : Set (Spec (CommRingCat.of A))) (hT : IsClosed T) (hTc : IsCompact Tᶜ) :
    ∃ G : DerivedCategory (Spec (CommRingCat.of A)).Modules,
      Stacks.Duality.quasiCoherentSupported (Spec (CommRingCat.of A)) T G ∧
        IsPerfect (X := (Spec (CommRingCat.of A)).toRingedSpace) G ∧
        ∀ E : DerivedCategory (Spec (CommRingCat.of A)).Modules,
          Stacks.Duality.quasiCoherentSupported (Spec (CommRingCat.of A)) T E →
            (∀ n : ℤ, Subsingleton (G⟦n⟧ ⟶ E)) → IsZero E := by
  obtain ⟨r, f, hfT⟩ := exists_openComplement_eq_compl T hT hTc
  exact ⟨koszulObject f, quasiCoherentSupported_koszulObject f T hfT,
    Stacks.Koszul.Truncation.isPerfect_koszulObject f,
    fun E hE horth => isZero_of_subsingleton_hom_koszulObject f T hfT E hE horth⟩

/-- **The affine base case of [Stacks, Tag 0A9A], read inside `D_{QCoh,T}(𝒪_{Spec A})`.** The
generator produced by `Stacks.Rouquier.exists_isPerfect_generator_supported_spec` is a weak
triangulated generator of the subcategory, in the `CategoryTheory.ObjectProperty.singleton`
spelling. -/
theorem exists_isPerfect_isWeakTriangulatedGenerator_supported_spec {A : Type u} [CommRing A]
    (T : Set (Spec (CommRingCat.of A))) (hT : IsClosed T) (hTc : IsCompact Tᶜ) :
    ∃ G : Stacks.Duality.QuasiCoherentSupportedDerivedCategory (Spec (CommRingCat.of A)) T,
      IsPerfect (X := (Spec (CommRingCat.of A)).toRingedSpace) G.obj ∧
        (ObjectProperty.singleton G).IsWeakTriangulatedGenerator := by
  obtain ⟨G, hGmem, hGperf, hGdet⟩ := exists_isPerfect_generator_supported_spec T hT hTc
  refine ⟨⟨G, hGmem⟩, hGperf, ?_⟩
  refine (@ObjectProperty.isWeakTriangulatedGenerator_singleton_iff _ _ _ _
    (Stacks.Duality.quasiCoherentSupported (Spec (CommRingCat.of A)) T)
    (Stacks.Duality.Supported.quasiCoherentSupported_isTriangulated
      (Spec (CommRingCat.of A)) T).toIsStableUnderShift ⟨G, hGmem⟩).2 ?_
  intro E hE hzero
  exact hGdet E hE fun n => ⟨fun g h => (hzero n g).trans (hzero n h).symm⟩

end Stacks.Rouquier

end
